<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Nov numbers in work fall to 34.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Nov numbers in work fall to 34.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN</p>
<p>NUMBERS IN WORK				Nov 96   Oct 96   Nov 95</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    34.474   34.638   34.975</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.252   34.315   34.750</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.291   34.352   34.792</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  28.221   28.343   28.589</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    28.045   28.085   28.412</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.295    6.341    6.431</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.246    6.267    6.380</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
